rain-core: xray/0054-muxcool-protocol-hardening
Source: ReClash fix on top of xray/0037 (GPL-3.0).

Only the client opens sessions. A server-initiated New frame is now ignored
with its payload, as Xray's client does, instead of being delivered as
ordinary stream data. Add codec fuzz targets over the golden corpus and the
malformed cases, protocol edge tests (maximum domain and payload, fragmented
input, multiple frames per read, keepalive, data after End, SessionID
exhaustion, writes after close), and benchmarks for the codec, the carrier
write turn and the pool/session paths. The uncontended write turn no longer
allocates a timer per frame; the deadline timer exists only while contended.
The benchmarks were also run against the pre-fix tree; the measured deltas are
recorded in the README.

Tests: FuzzDecodeFrame, FuzzDecodeFramePooled, TestServerInitiatedNewIsIgnored,
TestDecodeFrameAcceptsMaxDomainAndRejectsOverflow,
TestDecodeFrameAcceptsMaxPayload, TestDecodeFrameHandlesFragmentedInput,
TestDecodeFrameReadsOneFrameFromBufferedChunk, TestWorkerSessionIDExhaustion.
